Name: CPython embedded runtime
Short Name: cpython
URL: https://www.python.org/
Version: 3.13.18
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: PSF-2.0, MIT
License File: src/LICENSE, src/Doc/license.rst
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Description:
Source-built Windows x64 GIL runtime for the experimental native Python MVP.
Source: https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.18/Python-3.13.18.tar.xz
Archive SHA-256: abb0102e6d4ae027509bcb82327d9dd85515b44a3ba8ad538cfc5e9847029f68

Local Modifications:
src/ is an unmodified source subset selected by import_source.py. Its per-file
SHA-256 hashes are recorded in source_manifest.json. Build inputs are derived
from the upstream PCbuild/_freeze_module.vcxproj. Upstream tests, tools and
unused extension sources are not part of the subset.

mathmodule.c is also statically selected, with its upstream clinic and internal
headers. It uses the existing PSF license and Windows CRT math functions; it adds
no runtime DLL discovery, disk stdlib, site-packages, or random module. Game
replay uses a separately documented seeded xorshift32 in the Python sample.

GN builds a private static core inside one python_runtime.dll, and a separate
build-time freezer using the same pinned compiler. Frozen bootstrapping and
encoding modules are enumerated in frozen_modules.json; no on-disk stdlib is
shipped. Native extension loading is disabled in the generated Windows config.
embedded_getpath.c replaces path discovery with a strict explicit-path check;
builtin_modules.c defines the selected built-in table. embedded_buildinfo.c
supplies deterministic build metadata; sys._vpath is empty. Upstream source files
are not patched. Host build Python never generates target-version bytecode.

The private interpreter core uses optimize_speed even in a Chromium Debug build.
Symbols and normal compiler/linker diagnostics remain enabled. The embedding
and Chromium targets retain their selected build mode and execution budgets.

embedded_bootstrap_hash.c redirects CPython's BCryptGenRandom calls through
embedded_entropy.cc to base::RandBytes, whose Windows ProcessPrng path works in
the renderer sandbox. Hash seeds remain random; no sandbox policy is relaxed.

The nt/winreg/_io and other bootstrap builtins contain OS capabilities. This
runtime is NOT a language security sandbox. The embedder's private PythonScript
experiment is disabled by default. Restricted mode requires an exact configured
loopback origin, an eligible top-level document and existing script/CSP checks.
The browser user can explicitly relax ordinary page/origin/script checks in
Kernel Debug settings; this never changes the Renderer sandbox or OS privileges.
Its dom module exposes only opaque element handles and restricted text writes.
Execution/cleanup budgets are cooperative; there is no import security sandbox
or hard time/memory limit.
